WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.370
- Elon Musk is going to trial over Twitter

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:04.530
and fast, really fast.

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:06.300
Twitter wanted to go to trial in September

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:08.520
as in just a few days away.

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:10.830
But the chancellor, AKA the
judge, sided with Twitter

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:14.670
and set the trial for October
as in, also not very far away.

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:17.970
Elon Musk wanted to set the
trial for February, 2023,

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:19.710
which was very close to the expiration

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:21.180
of the financing obligations

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:23.100
and that might have been a
bid to blow up the whole deal.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.150
If you don't have financing,

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:25.680
maybe you can't go forward with it.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.230
And Musk wanted extra time
for extensive discovery

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:31.050
related to his too many
bots on Twitter theory

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:32.460
but that's not really relevant

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:35.460
to whether this particular
deal needs to close.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:37.830
So this is generally
bad news for Elon Musk

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:39.270
and good news for Twitter.

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:40.140
This is fast.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.442
And as I've said before,

00:00:41.442 --> 00:00:44.393
don't mess around with the
Delaware Chancery courts

00:00:44.393 --> 00:00:47.043
or you might find out,
just like Elon Musk did.

